[{"page":1,"text":"Public Notice\n\nVineyard City Announces Appointment of New City Council Member\nVineyard City is pleased to announce the appointment of Christopher Price to serve on the Vineyard City\n\nCouncil.\nFollowing the resignation of City Council member, Ezra Nair, the City conducted the vacancy appointment\nprocess in accordance with Utah law governing municipal vacancies, including public notice, review of\nqualified applicants, and consideration in an open public meeting.\nAt its public meeting held on September 15, 2026, the City Council voted to appoint Christopher Price to fill\nthe vacant council seat and serve the remainder of the unexpired term.\nMr. Price brings a commitment to public service and community involvement and will work alongside the\nMayor and City Council in representing the residents of Vineyard and advancing the City's strategic priorities.\nFollowing his appointment, Mr. Price will take the Oath of Office and be officially seated as a member of the\n\nVineyard City Council.\nThe Mayor, City Council, and staff are grateful for Mr. Price’s willingness to serve the residents of Vineyard.\nWe look forward to working with him as we continue to address important community priorities and support\nthe City's ongoing success.\nWe extend our appreciation to all residents who expressed interest in serving the community through the\nappointment process.\n\nFor additional information, please contact:\n\nThe Office of the City Recorder, Robin Bond\n\nVineyard City\n\n125 East Main Street\n\nVineyard, UT 84059\n\nEmail: robinr@vineyardutah.gov\n\nPhone: (385) 338-5214 ext 1101\n\nEnd of Notice","ocr":false}]